GKE 2 node pools. Top finding: Node pool legacy is RUNNING_WITH_ERROR with 1 condition(s).

FINDINGS
1. [high/high] gke.nodepool.unhealthy: Node pool legacy is RUNNING_WITH_ERROR with 1 condition(s)
   why: GKE cannot keep the node pool at its size or manage its nodes, usually because of zone capacity or quota (GCE_STOCKOUT, quota exceeded), the node service account, or the subnet running out of addresses.
   evidence (status): <<untrusted source="status">> RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED: GCE_STOCKOUT: The zone europe-west1-b does not have enough resources available. <</untrusted>>
   fix: Fix the cause in the evidence: request quota, use another zone or machine type, or restore the node service account's roles (roles/container.defaultNodeServiceAccount).
   docs: https://cloud.google.com/kubernetes-engine/docs/troubleshooting
2. [medium/high] gke.nodepool.version_skew: Node pool legacy runs Kubernetes 1.31.9-gke.200, behind the control plane's 1.33.5-gke.1000
   why: Nodes may lag the control plane by a few minors, but each lagging minor must be upgraded before the next control-plane upgrade, and new features and fixes do not reach these nodes.
   evidence (status): <<untrusted source="status">> node pool version 1.31.9-gke.200, control plane 1.33.5-gke.1000 <</untrusted>>
   fix: Upgrade the node pool to the control plane's version (a surge upgrade that respects PodDisruptionBudgets), or enable auto-upgrade.
   docs: https://cloud.google.com/kubernetes-engine/versioning

